# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: sphincs-r1-haraka-bitmask-size
why: thash() lets haraka256() write its 32-byte output into bitmask[inblocks * SPX_N], which is only 16 bytes for
why: one block: a stack overflow (AddressSanitizer dynamic-stack-buffer-overflow, CI run 45581879065). Only the first
why: inblocks * SPX_N bytes of bitmask are used, so the patch hashes into the 32-byte outbuf of the same function
why: and copies those bytes; every signature is unchanged.
file: upstream/crypto_sign/sphincs-haraka-128s/hash_haraka.c
count: 1
find:         haraka256(bitmask, buf_tmp);
replace:         haraka256(outbuf, buf_tmp); memcpy(bitmask, outbuf, inblocks * SPX_N);
